Basic relationship:
The sequence {1, \inf, a_n} is said to have the limit a if, for every given $math{\e>0}, there exists a number $math{N_(\e)} such that for all $math{n>N_(\e)}, it holds that $math{|a_n-a|<\e}
Can be rewritten to $math{lim{n->\inf, a_n}=a}
Convergent: $math{lim{n->\inf, a_n} = A}
Divergent: $math{lim{n->\inf, a_n} = \inf}
